        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: তুচ্ছ",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "তুচ্ছ — tuchchhô — \"trifling; petty\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "একটা তুচ্ছ ব্যাপার নিয়ে দুই ভাই ঝগড়া করল। ekṭā tuchchhô bæpār niye dui bhāi jhôgṛā kôrlô. The two brothers quarrelled over a trifling matter."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "তুচ্ছ (tuchchhô) করা, to brush aside, to treat as nothing."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "তুচ্ছ (tuchchhô) is a tatsama, Sanskrit tuccha, \"empty, vain, small, trifling\" (Monier-Williams)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for describing what you lived and felt."
